  <!-- ── TOP BANNER ── -->
  <div class="top-banner">
    <div class="banner-overline">Global Health Crisis</div>
    <div class="banner-title">Malaria: A<br><span>Preventable</span> Killer</div>
    <div class="banner-subtitle">Over half a million people die from malaria every year — most of them children. Yet humanity has made&nbsp;extraordinary progress eliminating this disease from half the world. The tools exist. The question is&nbsp;will.</div>
    <div class="banner-badge">
      <span class="num">1,320</span>
      <div class="lbl">children die daily</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── POSTER BODY ── -->
  <div class="poster-body">

    <!-- HERO STAT -->
    <div class="hero-stat-block">
      <div class="hero-stat-number">1,320</div>
      <div class="hero-stat-right">
        <div class="hero-stat-title">Children Die From Malaria<br>Every Single Day</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-desc">That is one child every 65 seconds — from a disease we know how to prevent and treat.<br>Every single one of these deaths is preventable.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- KEY METRICS -->
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <div class="metric-tile">
        <div class="metric-value" style="color:#ef4444">&gt;500,000</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Annual Deaths (2010s)</div>
        <div class="metric-context">Per year — majority are children under 5</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-tile">
        <div class="metric-value" style="color:#f59e0b">Africa</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Hardest-Hit Continent</div>
        <div class="metric-context">Bears the overwhelming majority of global malaria deaths</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-tile">
        <div class="metric-value" style="color:#60a5fa">Under 5</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Most Vulnerable Age</div>
        <div class="metric-context">Children under 5 account for the highest share of deaths globally</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- HISTORICAL PROGRESS — COMPARE BARS -->
    <div class="section-card accent-amber compare-section full-width">
      <div class="section-label">Historical Progress</div>
      <div class="compare-title">From Half the World to a Quarter</div>
      <div class="compare-subtitle">Malaria once stretched across ~50% of Earth's land — including Europe, East Asia, and the Americas. Decades of public health campaigns, land drainage, and development have shrunk its reach to ~27% by 2002. This is not a tropical disease by nature: it was eliminated everywhere except the tropics.</div>
      <div class="compare-bars">
        <div class="bar-row">
          <div class="bar-era">~1900<br><span style="font-size:19px;color:#64748b;font-weight:400">Peak spread</span></div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:50%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#dc2626,#ef4444)">50% of world's land surface</div>
            <div class="bar-pct">Europe · Americas · East Asia · Australasia</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-note" style="color:#ef4444;font-size:22px;font-weight:700">Including parts of Illinois &amp; Ireland</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bar-row">
          <div class="bar-era">2002<br><span style="font-size:19px;color:#64748b;font-weight:400">After campaigns</span></div>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:27%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#b45309,#f59e0b)">27%</div>
            <div class="bar-pct">Reduced to tropical &amp; sub-tropical belt</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-note" style="color:#22c55e;font-size:22px;font-weight:700">↓ Nearly halved in a century</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:44px;display:flex;gap:48px">
        <div style="flex:1;background:rgba(245,158,11,0.06);border-radius:12px;padding:28px 32px">
          <div style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:10px">🦟 Insecticides</div>
          <div style="font-size:20px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6">Widespread mosquito control campaigns dramatically reduced transmission in temperate zones</div>
        </div>
        <div style="flex:1;background:rgba(245,158,11,0.06);border-radius:12px;padding:28px 32px">
          <div style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:10px">🏗 Land Use Change</div>
          <div style="font-size:20px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6">Drainage of swamplands destroyed mosquito breeding grounds across Europe and North America</div>
        </div>
        <div style="flex:1;background:rgba(245,158,11,0.06);border-radius:12px;padding:28px 32px">
          <div style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:10px">📈 Development</div>
          <div style="font-size:20px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6">Better housing, healthcare systems, and economic growth cut exposure and improved treatment access</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DEATH TREND CHART -->
    <div class="section-card accent-red chart-section full-width">
      <div class="section-label">Death Trends 2000–2023</div>
      <div class="chart-title">The Fight Against Malaria: Progress, Stall, and COVID Setback</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">Global malaria deaths fell steadily from 2000 to 2015 — then progress stalled. The COVID-19 pandemic disrupted health systems in 2020, causing a sharp spike. Estimates differ between WHO and IHME, but both tell the same story.</div>
      <div class="chart-area">
        <svg class="chart-svg" viewBox="0 0 2100 340" preserveAspectRatio="none">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="areaGrad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
              <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#ef4444" stop-opacity="0.25"/>
              <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#ef4444" stop-opacity="0.02"/>
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>
          <!-- Grid lines -->
          <line x1="80" y1="20" x2="80" y2="280" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.08)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <line x1="80" y1="280" x2="2060" y2="280" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.12)" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="80" y1="20" x2="2060" y2="20" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.04)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <line x1="80" y1="90" x2="2060" y2="90" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.04)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <line x1="80" y1="160" x2="2060" y2="160" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.04)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <line x1="80" y1="230" x2="2060" y2="230" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.04)" stroke-width="1"/>

          <!-- Y-axis labels -->
          <text x="68" y="25" text-anchor="end" fill="#475569" font-size="18" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">900k</text>
          <text x="68" y="95" text-anchor="end" fill="#475569" font-size="18" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">750k</text>
          <text x="68" y="165" text-anchor="end" fill="#475569" font-size="18" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">600k</text>
          <text x="68" y="235" text-anchor="end" fill="#475569" font-size="18" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">450k</text>
          <text x="68" y="285" text-anchor="end" fill="#475569" font-size="18" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">300k</text>

          <!-- Data: map year→x, deaths→y. X: 2000=80..2023=2060, Y: 900k=20..300k=280 -->
          <!-- Scale: x=(year-2000)*87+80, y=280-((deaths-300)/600*260) -->
          <!-- Data points (deaths in thousands): 2000:901,2002:845,2004:780,2006:720,2008:660,2010:607,2012:568,2014:520,2016:490,2018:510,2020:627,2022:578,2023:560 -->
